      "writtenOn": "2024-10-02T18:26:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am hesitant to make this change since it affects the SkImage\u0027s logical alpha type, and there are maybe clients that have been assuming it was `kPremul`. Ideally they wouldn\u0027t have any hard-coded expectations for this, and wouldn\u0027t matter for any regular image shading since the SkColorXformSteps handles everything.\n\nBut if there was a YUV image used as a raw shader, the provided rgba values to a wrapping shader would be changing from premul to unpremul. We also then deviate from how a Ganesh YUV image behaves. It seems pretty rare to be used that way, but I don\u0027t think the bug fix around the opaque dstAT requires us to change the SkImage\u0027s reported alpha type.\n\nWe\u0027d just have to add a `srcAT` variable that starts out as `imageToDraw-\u003ealphaType()` and switches from `kPremul` to `kUnpremul` but keeps `kOpaque` unmodified.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 93
      },
      "revId": "4603f30cfca2ed9c8a22ceb16ef6b64e57fbcd7f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c18a5705_be3f3d1f",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/KeyHelpers.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1859,
