      "writtenOn": "2024-10-02T18:26:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like for regular SkImage raw shaders, we don\u0027t do any canonicalization of the alpha type, you get whatever was in the texture, premul or unpremul.\n\nBefore this change, we were forcing the premul step to match the reported alpha type of the YUV SkImage. Now we are changing the raw shader behavior based on the dst alpha type, which doesn\u0027t seem right.\n\nIf you like the `srcAT` idea, I think this could always just be a conversion from `srcAT` to `imageToDraw-\u003ealphaType()`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1863,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1866,
        "endChar": 64
      },
